ield through online courses and self-learning. The following are the common educational qualifications required:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Bachelor\u2019s Degree:<\/strong> A degree in computer science, IT, mathematics, or a related field helps you build a strong foundation in programming, data analysis, and core concepts.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Master\u2019s Degree (Optional):<\/strong> Some candidates pursue a master\u2019s degree in data science, analytics, or <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/what-is-artificial-intelligence\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">artificial intelligence<\/a> to gain deeper knowledge and access better career opportunities.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Certifications &amp; Online Courses:<\/strong> Short-term courses help you learn practical skills, tools, and real-world applications used in the industry, making it easier to gain hands-on experience and build job-ready knowledge.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Become a Data Scientist After 12th in India?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>To become a data scientist after 12th, you can follow a simple roadmap: choose the right stream \u2192 select a relevant degree \u2192 learn key skills \u2192 practice with projects \u2192 gain internships \u2192 apply for jobs.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The journey usually begins with building a strong foundation in mathematics and logical thinking. After that, you can pursue a degree like B.Tech, B.Sc, or BCA in a related field. Along with your studies, start <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/python\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">learning Python,<\/a> <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/resources\/sql\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">SQL<\/a>, statistics, and basic machine learning concepts.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>The most important part is practical experience. Working on projects like data analysis or prediction models helps you build real skills. With consistent practice and hands-on experience, you can become ready for internships and entry-level roles.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Also Read<\/strong>: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-course-syllabus\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Science Course Syllabus: Fees, Duration, Eligibility, Details<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Skills Required to Become a Data Scientist<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>To become a data scientist, you need both technical skills and problem-solving abilities to work with data effectively. Below are the required skills:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1654\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-scientist-skills.webp\" alt=\"Data Scientist Skills\" class=\"wp-image-20468\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-scientist-skills.webp 1654w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-scientist-skills-300x181.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-scientist-skills-1024x619.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-scientist-skills-768x464.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/data-scientist-skills-1536x929.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1654px) 100vw, 1654px\" \/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Technical Skills<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong><a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/best-programming-languages\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Programming Languages<\/a> (Python\/R):<\/strong> Learn languages like Python or R to handle data, perform analysis, build models, and automate tasks efficiently in real-world <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-science-project-ideas\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">data science projects<\/a>.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Statistics and Mathematics:<\/strong> Understanding statistics, probability, and basic mathematics helps you analyze data, identify patterns, and make accurate predictions using logical and analytical approaches.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Analysis:<\/strong> Ability to clean, process, and analyze large datasets to extract useful insights and support business decisions using structured and unstructured data sources.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Visualization:<\/strong> Use tools such as charts and graphs to present data clearly, helping stakeholders understand insights and make better decisions.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Machine Learning:<\/strong>&nbsp; Knowledge of machine learning algorithms helps you build predictive models, automate decision-making processes, and improve the accuracy of data-driven solutions over time.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Database Management (SQL):<\/strong> You should understand SQL to efficiently store, manage, and retrieve data from databases, which is essential for handling large datasets in real-world projects.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Big Data Technologies:<\/strong> Familiarity with tools like Hadoop or Spark helps you process and analyze large volumes of data quickly and efficiently in distributed computing environments.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Data Cleaning and Preprocessing:<\/strong> Learn to handle missing data, remove errors, and prepare datasets for analysis, ensuring accurate and reliable results in data science projects.&nbsp;<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Soft Skills<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Problem-Solving Skills:<\/strong> Ability to identify problems, analyze data, and find effective solutions using logical thinking and a structured approach in real-world scenarios.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Communication Skills:<\/strong> Strong communication helps explain complex data insights in simple terms, making it easier for non-technical stakeholders to understand and make decisions.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Critical Thinking:<\/strong> You should evaluate data logically, question assumptions, and interpret results accurately to ensure reliable insights and better decision-making outcomes.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Business Understanding:<\/strong> Understanding business goals helps data scientists align their analysis with real-world problems and deliver insights that create real value for organizations.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Teamwork and Collaboration:<\/strong> Ability to work with cross-functional teams such as developers, analysts, and managers to complete projects efficiently and achieve common goals.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Time Management:<\/strong> Managing time effectively helps handle multiple tasks, meet deadlines, and complete projects without compromising quality or accuracy.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Adaptability:<\/strong> You need to continuously learn new tools, technologies, and techniques, as the data science field evolves rapidly with changing trends and innovations.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Attention to Detail:<\/strong> Paying close attention to data ensures accuracy, reduces errors, and improves the overall quality of analysis and decision-making processes.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">How to Become a Data Scientist? Step-by-Step<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Here are the important steps that you can follow to become a successful data scientist:<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"aligncenter size-full\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1654\" height=\"1000\" src=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/steps-to-become-data-scientist.webp\" alt=\"How to Become a Data Scientist? Step-by-Step\" class=\"wp-image-20469\" srcset=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/steps-to-become-data-scientist.webp 1654w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/steps-to-become-data-scientist-300x181.webp 300w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/steps-to-become-data-scientist-1024x619.webp 1024w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/steps-to-become-data-scientist-768x464.webp 768w, https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/steps-to-become-data-scientist-1536x929.webp 1536w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1654px) 100vw, 1654px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 1: Learn Basic Mathematics &amp; Statistics<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Start by learning basic mathematical concepts such as algebra, probability, and statistics, as they form the foundation of data science. These concepts help you understand data patterns, analyze results, and build accurate models for better decision-making.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 2: Learn Programming (Python\/R)<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Learning programming is an important step in becoming a data scientist. Languages like Python and R are widely used for data analysis, data manipulation, and building machine learning models. Python is especially popular because of its simple syntax and powerful libraries.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>You should focus on understanding basic concepts such as variables, loops, functions, and data structures. Practice using libraries like NumPy, Pandas, and Matplotlib to work with data efficiently and perform analysis in real-world projects.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 3: Understand Data Analysis<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Learn how to collect, clean, and process raw data to extract useful insights. You should understand techniques such as data wrangling, exploration, and interpretation that help you identify patterns, trends, and meaningful insights to support better decision-making.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 4: Learn Data Visualization<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Learn how to present data using charts, graphs, and dashboards to make complex information easy to understand. You should use visualization tools and libraries to highlight trends, patterns, and insights, helping stakeholders quickly interpret data and make informed decisions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 5: Master Machine Learning Concepts<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Machine learning is a core part of data science that allows systems to learn from data and make predictions. You should understand concepts such as supervised and unsupervised learning, along with basic algorithms such as regression, classification, and clustering.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Focus on how models are trained, tested, and improved for better accuracy. Learning concepts like overfitting, underfitting, and model evaluation helps you build reliable and effective machine learning models for real-world problems.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 6: Work on Real Projects<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Working on real projects helps you apply your knowledge to practical problems. It improves your skills in data analysis, machine learning, and visualization. Building projects also strengthens your portfolio and demonstrates your abilities to employers, increasing your chances of getting job opportunities.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 7: Build a Strong Portfolio<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Create a strong portfolio by showcasing your projects, code, and problem-solving skills. Include real-world projects, case studies, and clear explanations to show your abilities. A well-organized portfolio helps employers understand your skills and increases your chances of getting hired.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Step 8: Apply for Internships and Jobs<\/h3>\n\n\n\n<p>Start applying for internships and entry-level data science roles to gain practical experience. Internships help you understand real-world projects, work with teams, and improve your technical and problem-solving skills in a professional environment.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Prepare a strong resume, update your portfolio, and practice interview questions regularly. Apply on job portals and company websites to increase your chances of getting selected and starting your data science career.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>Read in Detail<\/strong>: <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/data-scientist-roadmap\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Data Scientist Roadmap: A Guide for Beginners<\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">Challenges in Becoming a Data Scientist and How to Overcome Them<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Below are some challenges faced while becoming a data scientist:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li><strong>Learning Multiple Skills:<\/strong> Data science requires knowledge of programming, statistics, and machine learning, which can feel overwhelming for beginners trying to learn all of it at once.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Handling Large Datasets:<\/strong> Working with large, complex datasets can be challenging, especially when cleaning, processing, and analyzing them efficiently. It requires proper tools, techniques, and skills to extract meaningful insights accurately and effectively.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Understanding Complex Concepts:<\/strong> Topics such as machine learning algorithms, data modeling, and advanced statistics can be difficult to grasp without proper guidance and consistent practice.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Lack of Practical Experience:<\/strong> Many beginners struggle due to limited hands-on experience, making it difficult to apply theoretical knowledge to real-world data problems effectively.<br><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Keeping Up with New Technologies:<\/strong> The data science field evolves rapidly, and staying up to date with new tools, technologies, and trends can be challenging.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<p><strong>How to Overcome Them:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Start with basics and learn step-by-step instead of trying to learn everything at once.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Practice regularly by working on real-world projects and datasets.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use online resources, tutorials, and communities for continuous learning.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Break complex topics into smaller parts for better understanding.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Stay consistent and keep updating your skills with new tools and technologies.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n        <div class=\"container position-relative mb-2\">\n            <div class=\"row pb-4\">\n                <h2 style=\"font-size:32px\">Upcoming Masterclass<\/h2>\n                <p>Attend our live classes led by experienced and desiccated instructors of Wscube Tech.<\/p>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"owl-carousel myOwl\">\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/cracking-meta-google-ads-2026-data-automation-attribution?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-07-31T112145_393_1785491880854_775860.webp\" alt=\"Cracking Meta &amp; Google Ads 2026 - Data, Automation &amp; Attribution\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/ai-engineering-roadmap-2026?utm_source=WsBlog&#038;utm_medium=blog_master_class_slider&#038;utm_campaign=SEO\" target=\"_blank\">\n                    <img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/deen3evddmddt.cloudfront.net\/uploads\/master-class-media\/1a_-_2026-07-31T123426_340_1785490284771_211381.webp\" alt=\"AI Engineering Roadmap 2026\" \/>\n                <\/a>\n            <\/div>\n            <div class=\"item\">\n                <a href=\"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/events\/how-to-build-an-ai-agent-from-scratch?utm_