st collects, cleans, and analyzes large amounts of data to extract meaningful insights. You build models, identify patterns, and create visualizations to help organizations make data-driven decisions and solve real-world problems effectively.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695698754","position":2,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695698754","name":"2. What qualifications are needed to become a data scientist?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A degree in computer science, mathematics, statistics, or a related field is helpful, but strong practical skills, certifications, and project experience are equally important for building a successful data science career.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695710766","position":3,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695710766","name":"3. Can I become a data scientist without coding?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Basic coding knowledge is essential in data science, especially in Python or R, as most tasks like data analysis, visualization, and machine learning require programming skills to work efficiently.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695721682","position":4,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695721682","name":"4. Is data science a good career option?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, data science is a highly rewarding career with strong demand, high salaries, and growth opportunities, as companies across industries rely heavily on data-driven decision-making and advanced analytics.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695735733","position":5,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695735733","name":"5. How long does it take to become a data scientist?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The time required depends on your background and learning pace, but generally, it takes around 6 months to 2 years to become job-ready with consistent learning, practice, and real-world project experience.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695747538","position":6,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695747538","name":"6. Can I become a data scientist after 12th?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, you can start after 12th by choosing a relevant degree and learning essential skills like programming, statistics, and data analysis, while building projects and gaining practical experience over time.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695760950","position":7,"url":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-data-scientist\/#faq-question-1774695760950","name":"7. Which programming language is best for data science?","answerCount":1,"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Python is widely preferred in data science because it is easy to learn and has many useful libraries, while R is commonly used for statistical analysis and creating data visualizations.","inLanguage":"en-US"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"Question","@id":"https:\/\/www.wscubetech.com\/blog\/how-to-become-da